cat > CONTRIBUTING.md <<'SOA_EOF_eca12c0a30e25b4b'
# Contributing to SOA

SOA is a multi-tenant document-operations product. Changes must preserve evidence, deterministic validation, tenant boundaries, and replayability—not merely make a demo appear to work.

## Local setup

```bash
cp .env.example .env
make install
make dev
```

Use the synthetic sample documents in `sample-data/`. Never commit customer documents, provider keys, database files, or exported payloads.

## Required checks

Before opening a pull request:

```bash
make check
```

For changes that touch ingestion, extraction, validation, review, or job orchestration, also run:

```bash
make smoke
```

## Architectural invariants

- Every tenant-owned record and operation is organization-scoped on the server.
- Uploaded documents are untrusted content; they never become instructions or gain arbitrary tool/network access.
- OCR and LLM providers remain behind adapters and return the canonical schema.
- Every field presented for approval retains source evidence and extraction provenance.
- Processing stages are idempotent and retry-safe.
- Blocking validation errors cannot be silently approved; supervisor overrides require a reason and audit event.
- Schema, prompt, rule, provider, and workflow changes must be versionable and regression-testable.
- Local SQLite/filesystem mode and PostgreSQL/S3-compatible mode must remain supported through configuration, not forks.

## Pull request expectations

A pull request should explain the user impact, architecture impact, test evidence, migration requirements, security implications, and rollback path. UI changes should include relevant states: loading, empty, error, permission denied, low confidence, validation failure, and success.

The canonical implementation contract is [`docs/MASTER_BUILD_PLAN.md`](docs/MASTER_BUILD_PLAN.md).
SOA_EOF_eca12c0a30e25b4b

cat > Makefile <<'SOA_EOF_76ed074a9305c040'
SHELL := /bin/bash

.PHONY: help install dev api web worker test lint format build check smoke migrate seed compose-up compose-down

help:
	@echo "SOA commands"
	@echo "  make install      Install API and web dependencies"
	@echo "  make dev          Run API, worker, and web locally"
	@echo "  make test         Run backend and frontend tests"
	@echo "  make lint         Run Ruff and TypeScript checks"
	@echo "  make build        Build the production web bundle"
	@echo "  make check        Run lint, tests, migration check, and build"
	@echo "  make smoke        Run the synthetic end-to-end API smoke test"
	@echo "  make compose-up   Start the complete Docker stack"

install:
	python3 -m venv .venv
	. .venv/bin/activate && pip install -e 'apps/api[dev]'
	cd apps/web && npm install

api:
	. .venv/bin/activate && cd apps/api && uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000

worker:
	. .venv/bin/activate && cd apps/api && python -m app.worker

web:
	cd apps/web && npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0

dev:
	./scripts/dev.sh

test:
	. .venv/bin/activate && cd apps/api && pytest
	cd apps/web && npm test -- --run

lint:
	. .venv/bin/activate && cd apps/api && ruff check app tests alembic && ruff format --check app tests alembic
	cd apps/web && npm run typecheck

format:
	. .venv/bin/activate && cd apps/api && ruff format app tests alembic
	cd apps/web && npm run format

build:
	cd apps/web && npm run build

migrate:
	. .venv/bin/activate && cd apps/api && alembic upgrade head

check: lint test build
	@tmp_db="data/migration-check-$$(date +%s).db"; \
	cd apps/api && mkdir -p data && \
	APP_ENV=development SECRET_KEY=local-check-secret-with-more-than-thirty-two-characters DATABASE_URL="sqlite:///./$$tmp_db" ../../.venv/bin/alembic upgrade head && \
	APP_ENV=development SECRET_KEY=local-check-secret-with-more-than-thirty-two-characters DATABASE_URL="sqlite:///./$$tmp_db" ../../.venv/bin/alembic check && \
	rm -f "$$tmp_db"

smoke:
	. .venv/bin/activate && python scripts/smoke_test.py

seed:
	. .venv/bin/activate && cd apps/api && python -m app.seed

compose-up:
	docker compose up --build

compose-down:
	docker compose down -v
SOA_EOF_76ed074a9305c040

cat > README.md <<'SOA_EOF_b335630551682c19'
# SOA — Document Operations Platform

SOA is a local-first, multi-tenant B2B intelligent document processing platform. The first production workflow converts incoming purchase orders into validated, reviewable, ERP-ready sales orders. The same platform primitives support invoices, remittances, delivery documents, claims, and other document streams.

## What is implemented

- Multi-tenant organizations, roles, processes, and location-specific streams
- Upload and asynchronous processing for PDF and image documents
- Native PDF text extraction plus Tesseract OCR fallback
- Local OpenAI-compatible model support